WEBVTT

00:00:16.141 --> 00:00:17.059
What are you--?

00:00:17.059 --> 00:00:19.603
Stay just like that.

00:00:19.603 --> 00:00:20.729
So beautiful.

00:00:20.729 --> 00:00:23.190
Huh? What's gotten into you?

00:00:24.608 --> 00:00:28.070
Sorawo, your right eye is so blue.

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:31.365
Check this out.

00:00:31.365 --> 00:00:34.535
It's translucent. How'd you do that?

00:00:34.535 --> 00:00:37.538
Come on, it's not like I could do it on purpose.

00:00:37.538 --> 00:00:41.667
I bet it happened when we
hunted down that wiggle-waggle!

00:01:32.551 --> 00:01:33.719
"Kisaragi"
"Katasu - Yami"

00:02:12.674 --> 00:02:17.930
Three days ago, we encountered
a creature known as a wiggle-waggle

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:20.599
and barely managed to defeat it.

00:02:20.599 --> 00:02:23.769
The wiggle-waggle urban
legend is well known on the net.

00:02:23.769 --> 00:02:28.941
They're said to be creatures that
drive you mad just by looking at them.

00:02:28.941 --> 00:02:34.571
I believe my right eye turned blue
because I looked at one for too long.

00:02:34.571 --> 00:02:38.617
If so, then Toriko's left hand
probably turned translucent

00:02:38.617 --> 00:02:45.082
when she yanked off those things
that were growing around my eyes.

00:02:47.084 --> 00:02:49.378
Let's have an expert take a look.

00:02:49.378 --> 00:02:52.714
I know a researcher who
specializes in the Otherside.

00:02:52.714 --> 00:02:54.591
A researcher?

00:02:54.591 --> 00:03:00.097
Yeah, that's who wants the mirror
cubes that the wiggle-waggles drop.

00:03:00.097 --> 00:03:04.268
An Otherside... researcher?

00:03:07.646 --> 00:03:09.898
I hate to have to ask this, but...

00:03:09.898 --> 00:03:13.527
You're not ripping off that researcher, are you?

00:03:13.527 --> 00:03:16.613
Why do you say that?
I'm just bringing the cubes from that side,

00:03:16.613 --> 00:03:18.949
and the researcher is paying
a ton of money for them.

00:03:18.949 --> 00:03:21.827
Maybe I'm the one getting ripped off.

00:03:29.835 --> 00:03:32.004
This is...

00:03:32.004 --> 00:03:35.382
...that place the neighborhood
kids say is haunted.

00:03:35.382 --> 00:03:37.801
Hello?

00:03:46.018 --> 00:03:48.187
We're here!

00:03:48.187 --> 00:03:52.107
Keep it down. Hurry up and get in here.

00:03:52.107 --> 00:03:56.153
Huh? Um, wait a sec!

00:03:56.153 --> 00:03:59.531
Sorry for calling out of the blue.

00:04:04.536 --> 00:04:05.704
Who're you?

00:04:05.704 --> 00:04:08.498
Oh, that's my friend Sorawo.

00:04:08.498 --> 00:04:10.918
H-Hi, I'm Sorawo Kamikoshi--

00:04:10.918 --> 00:04:14.129
She's your friend? How much did you pay her?

00:04:14.129 --> 00:04:16.381
Nothing, she's free.

00:04:16.381 --> 00:04:18.217
Sorawo, sit. Make yourself at home.

00:04:18.217 --> 00:04:21.261
Don't try to run the show. This is my place.

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:24.473
She's the one I was talking about.
Her name is Kozakura,

00:04:24.473 --> 00:04:27.017
and she conducts research related
to cognitive science and the Otherside.

00:04:27.017 --> 00:04:30.687
She's a complete stranger.
What have you been telling her about me?

00:04:30.687 --> 00:04:34.650
I said you were an expert on the Otherside.

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:38.654
An expert, huh? So your name's Sorawo?

00:04:38.654 --> 00:04:40.280
Sit.

00:04:42.324 --> 00:04:44.368
You met on the Otherside?

00:04:44.368 --> 00:04:48.580
Yeah. And check this out.

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:50.290
Yikes! You're freaking me out!

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:54.169
It's not only me. Look at Sorawo's eye.

00:04:57.548 --> 00:05:01.009
That's a real eye, all right. What happened?

00:05:01.009 --> 00:05:05.848
Um... Ever hear of the wiggle-waggle
urban legend that's all over the net?

00:05:05.848 --> 00:05:08.517
Not really. Care to explain?

00:05:08.517 --> 00:05:13.814
Well, this is what happens
when you stare at one too long.

00:05:13.814 --> 00:05:18.068
I ended up like this when I touched
Sorawo while she was under its power.

00:05:18.068 --> 00:05:19.611
That means...

00:05:19.611 --> 00:05:23.198
...you've both had a close
encounter of the fourth kind!

00:05:23.198 --> 00:05:27.828
You have some nerve barging in here
uninvited and touching everything!

00:05:27.828 --> 00:05:29.872
You said we could come in.

00:05:29.872 --> 00:05:32.416
Um, what's the fourth kind?

00:05:35.043 --> 00:05:38.172
In ufology, contact events
with UFOs are classified

00:05:38.172 --> 00:05:41.633
as close encounters of the
first, second, and third kind.

00:05:41.633 --> 00:05:46.847
I've applied a similar scale to
contact events with the Otherside.

00:05:46.847 --> 00:05:52.728
The fourth kind has
a physical impact on the body.

00:05:52.728 --> 00:05:55.981
The closer the contact with the
Otherside, the greater the danger.

00:05:55.981 --> 00:05:58.984
Some contactees are enthralled by the Otherside.

00:05:58.984 --> 00:06:01.361
It becomes an addiction, and they never return.

00:06:01.361 --> 00:06:04.740
Like Satsuki.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:05.782
Is that--

00:06:05.782 --> 00:06:09.536
She disappeared over there.
She was... my friend.

00:06:09.536 --> 00:06:13.707
I was friends with Satsuki first.

00:06:13.707 --> 00:06:15.292
We were classmates in college.

00:06:15.292 --> 00:06:23.258
She somehow learned of the Otherside
and dragged me into her research.

00:06:23.258 --> 00:06:25.219
Have you been there, too?

00:06:25.219 --> 00:06:30.516
No, I've never actually gone.
I tried to stop her because of the risk.

00:06:30.516 --> 00:06:33.727
Then one day, she said she'd
found an enthusiastic assistant

00:06:33.727 --> 00:06:35.729
and brought Toriko over to meet me.

00:06:35.729 --> 00:06:43.111
Satsuki had been my tutor.
In time, she told me about the Otherside.

00:06:43.111 --> 00:06:46.657
We ended up exploring it together.

00:06:46.657 --> 00:06:50.369
But I lost all contact
with her three months ago.

00:06:50.369 --> 00:06:55.249
I was worried, so I searched
for her many times, but...

00:06:55.249 --> 00:06:57.793
Even after I warned you
it was crazy to do it alone.

00:06:57.793 --> 00:07:00.754
She's our friend. We have to help her!

00:07:00.754 --> 00:07:03.841
Oh, I almost forgot.

00:07:03.841 --> 00:07:05.968
Look what I brought.

00:07:10.305 --> 00:07:12.349
It's bigger than the last one.

00:07:12.349 --> 00:07:14.768
It wasn't easy getting it.

00:07:18.397 --> 00:07:19.982
Thanks!

00:07:21.108 --> 00:07:24.820
Now, about my left hand and
Sorawo's right eye. What are we gonna--

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:28.740
I'm a cognitive scientist, not a medical doctor.

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:33.078
Ahhh...

00:07:33.078 --> 00:07:35.372
It feels so good after it rains.

00:07:35.372 --> 00:07:38.250
I wonder if we'll see a rainbow.

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:39.668
This is for you.

00:07:39.668 --> 00:07:44.298
Are you good with a 50-50 split?
Now you can get your phone fixed.

00:07:46.049 --> 00:07:47.467
Okay.

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:51.263
I never thanked you, did I? So, thanks, Sorawo.

00:07:51.263 --> 00:07:52.973
Oh, no, I should thank--

00:07:52.973 --> 00:07:55.100
So, when should we go again?

00:07:55.100 --> 00:08:00.814
Again? Hold on! We haven't figured out
what happened to my eye or your hand!

00:08:00.814 --> 00:08:03.650
Shouldn't we have pressed
a little harder for some answers?

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:07.613
Kozakura said she didn't know,
so we shouldn't question her.

00:08:07.613 --> 00:08:10.199
I'm sure she'll let us know
if she discovers something.

00:08:10.199 --> 00:08:11.742
Can we trust her?

00:08:11.742 --> 00:08:15.621
Yes. After all, Satsuki did.

00:08:15.621 --> 00:08:19.374
You were really close to Satsuki, weren't you?

00:08:19.374 --> 00:08:22.294
Yeah, no one's more important to me.

00:08:22.294 --> 00:08:27.132
But if I'm honest, I was scared
to go over there on my own.

00:08:27.132 --> 00:08:31.803
So I was so happy when
I ran into you. Like, super happy!

00:08:31.803 --> 00:08:33.514
O-Oh...

00:08:33.514 --> 00:08:35.599
When we defeated that wiggle-waggle,

00:08:35.599 --> 00:08:40.729
I realized I might never find Satsuki on my own,
but maybe I could with you, Sorawo.

00:08:45.692 --> 00:08:47.986
I'll be in touch again tomorrow.

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:54.701
Leave me out of this.

00:08:59.873 --> 00:09:02.668
And here I am.

00:09:04.378 --> 00:09:05.629
Sorawo.

00:09:05.629 --> 00:09:06.672
Been waiting long?

00:09:06.672 --> 00:09:07.673
Fifteen minutes.

00:09:07.673 --> 00:09:11.552
Wrong answer.
You're supposed to say, "I just got here."

00:09:11.552 --> 00:09:14.096
What is this, a date?

00:09:19.935 --> 00:09:21.770
Did you bring your gun?

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:23.438
Just in case.

00:09:55.846 --> 00:10:00.934
So, where to? Any idea
where Satsuki might've gone?

00:10:00.934 --> 00:10:04.438
She wasn't the type to discuss her plans.

00:10:04.438 --> 00:10:06.231
You're no help.

00:10:09.359 --> 00:10:12.279
From above, I could see what looks like
an abandoned building to the southwest.

00:10:12.279 --> 00:10:14.656
Ever been there?

00:10:14.656 --> 00:10:19.453
Then let's go have a look.
If she's too injured to move,

00:10:19.453 --> 00:10:22.915
she may've sought shelter
where there's a roof over her head.

00:10:25.542 --> 00:10:28.295
Is there something wrong?

00:10:28.295 --> 00:10:32.508
No, it's just, you're so
focused on finding your friend

00:10:32.508 --> 00:10:35.010
but haven't given any thought to how to do it.

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:37.596
I know I shouldn't rush into this,

00:10:37.596 --> 00:10:42.059
but when I think how Satsuki
could be in danger, I had to act.

00:10:42.059 --> 00:10:45.437
Hmph. Then I hope we find her soon.

00:10:45.437 --> 00:10:48.857
Sorawo, I don't care for that attitude.

00:10:50.275 --> 00:10:54.488
Would you stop sulking and acting like a child?

00:10:54.488 --> 00:10:57.074
Like a child? I could say the same about y--

00:10:57.074 --> 00:10:58.784
Stop!

00:11:14.716 --> 00:11:15.884
Drop the weapon!

00:11:15.884 --> 00:11:19.847
Go any farther and you'll end up dead.
This place is full of glitches.

00:11:19.847 --> 00:11:22.724
Glitches? Whatever, just drop your gun.

00:11:22.724 --> 00:11:26.478
No can do. I just saved your life.

00:11:28.856 --> 00:11:30.315
Watch.

00:11:42.411 --> 00:11:43.745
What just happened?

00:11:43.745 --> 00:11:47.958
Step there and it'll be the last step
you ever take. You'll be turned to ash.

00:11:47.958 --> 00:11:49.585
What's a glitch?

00:11:49.585 --> 00:11:56.175
It's a supernatural trap.
Forging blindly ahead is suici--

00:11:57.759 --> 00:12:00.971
You're... Michiko?

00:12:02.806 --> 00:12:07.394
I've been looking for you!
Ever since you suddenly vanished!

00:12:07.394 --> 00:12:08.604
Oh, what a relief.

00:12:08.604 --> 00:12:08.729
--No, wait.

00:12:08.729 --> 00:12:10.230
--Michiko.
--No, wait.

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:10.480
--What's the matter?
--No, wait.

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:12.524
--What's the matter?
--Back off!

00:12:13.734 --> 00:12:16.361
You're not... Michiko?

00:12:16.361 --> 00:12:21.116
That's right. We're not
whoever you're looking for.

00:12:21.116 --> 00:12:23.869
Oh, I lost it there for a second.

00:12:27.331 --> 00:12:28.790
Mr. Abarato?

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:30.959
I'm really sorry.

00:12:30.959 --> 00:12:34.213
I've been looking for
my wife here in this world.

00:12:34.213 --> 00:12:36.256
Your wife?

00:12:36.256 --> 00:12:39.885
She was spirited away.

00:12:39.885 --> 00:12:42.179
Spirited away.

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:47.267
Folklore is full of tales about people
disappearing without warning.

00:12:47.267 --> 00:12:52.856
There are endless variations
throughout history and across the world.

00:12:52.856 --> 00:12:54.942
It happened one summer night.

00:12:54.942 --> 00:13:01.073
We had finished dinner and
were talking about watching a movie.

00:13:01.073 --> 00:13:02.866
I was in another part of the house

00:13:02.866 --> 00:13:05.994
when I asked what movie she was
in the mood for but got no response.

00:13:05.994 --> 00:13:12.668
She'd been in the living room just
20 seconds earlier but suddenly vanished.

00:13:12.668 --> 00:13:15.128
I considered every possibility,

00:13:15.128 --> 00:13:17.881
including physical abduction
and unexplained disappearance.

00:13:17.881 --> 00:13:21.134
But I now believe it had
to be a supernatural event.

00:13:21.134 --> 00:13:25.264
My wife was taken away to another world.

00:13:25.264 --> 00:13:27.975
I poured through fairy tales,
folktales, and legends

00:13:27.975 --> 00:13:30.978
for any information on where
those who are spirited away go.

00:13:30.978 --> 00:13:34.064
And I sought endlessly for clues
to making contact with the other world.

00:13:34.064 --> 00:13:37.943
Finally, I came across what I call the Zone.

00:13:37.943 --> 00:13:41.446
I'd heard rumors of people
disappearing at a forsaken shrine

00:13:41.446 --> 00:13:43.240
in the mountains of Chichibu.

00:13:43.240 --> 00:13:46.451
When I passed through its Torii gate,
a grassland appeared before me

00:13:46.451 --> 00:13:49.580
like a phantasmal vision.

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:54.877
I found I could go there by passing
through at the right time and angle.

00:13:56.086 --> 00:13:57.963
Why are you two here?

00:13:57.963 --> 00:14:02.050
Same as you. Someone dear
to me vanished here in this world.

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:07.181
Oh, wow. Really? I know how hard it is
when someone you care for vanishes.

00:14:07.181 --> 00:14:08.223
R-Right...

00:14:08.223 --> 00:14:09.725
Thanks.

00:14:09.725 --> 00:14:11.143
Now you're empathizing with him?

00:14:11.143 --> 00:14:17.649
It seems you're not familiar with the Zone.
I'll show you the safest route.

00:14:21.028 --> 00:14:23.906
Have you met anyone else in this world?

00:14:23.906 --> 00:14:28.202
I'm looking for a tall girl
with long, black hair.

00:14:28.202 --> 00:14:30.996
I'm afraid that doesn't ring a bell.

00:14:30.996 --> 00:14:35.209
I rarely encounter anyone in the Zone,
and when I do, I try to stay away.

00:14:35.209 --> 00:14:37.544
Why?

00:14:37.544 --> 00:14:40.255
Because it might be "them."

00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:43.675
They're everywhere.

00:14:43.675 --> 00:14:48.472
They sneak into our world to
tap our phones and steal our mail.

00:14:48.472 --> 00:14:50.807
It's no use reporting it to the police.

00:14:50.807 --> 00:14:53.894
They already have people on the inside.

00:14:53.894 --> 00:14:55.687
Um...

00:14:55.687 --> 00:14:57.856
Who exactly do you mean by "them"?

00:14:57.856 --> 00:15:03.529
The denizens of the Zone.
They sneak into our world and abduct people.

00:15:03.529 --> 00:15:07.115
They... took my wife away from me.

00:15:07.115 --> 00:15:10.369
How can you tell we're not one of them?

00:15:10.369 --> 00:15:13.622
You guys were arguing when we met.

00:15:13.622 --> 00:15:19.211
You'd never see them do that.
They don't have emotions like humans do.

00:15:20.504 --> 00:15:22.548
Footprints.

00:15:26.051 --> 00:15:28.095
Let's follow them.

00:15:29.513 --> 00:15:31.431
Is it a good idea to go with him?

00:15:31.431 --> 00:15:36.854
I'm going, even if there's the
slimmest chance of finding Satsuki.

00:15:38.105 --> 00:15:44.194
Yeah, I get it. I hope they
each find who they're looking for.

00:15:44.194 --> 00:15:46.446
But it doesn't have anything to do with me.

00:15:46.446 --> 00:15:50.784
I wanted to be alone here on the Otherside.

00:15:50.784 --> 00:15:53.912
Sorawo, hurry.

00:15:53.912 --> 00:15:56.248
That's all I wanted.

00:16:04.006 --> 00:16:05.799
They lead into this building.

00:16:05.799 --> 00:16:07.342
Yeah.

00:16:14.099 --> 00:16:18.896
This... isn't a human footprint.

00:16:30.908 --> 00:16:34.286
You were really close to Satsuki, weren't you?

00:16:34.286 --> 00:16:37.331
Yeah, no one's more important to me.

00:16:37.331 --> 00:16:45.005
No, you fool. Toriko...
Whoever's in there, it's not Satsuki.

00:16:57.893 --> 00:17:01.480
Lady Hasshaku... There are stories
about people being attacked

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:05.943
by a woman over six and a half feet tall
and wearing a white sundress.

00:17:05.943 --> 00:17:08.070
I knew Satsuki was here.

00:17:08.070 --> 00:17:10.697
Toriko? Wait!

00:17:15.577 --> 00:17:17.454
Wait, Toriko!

00:17:17.454 --> 00:17:20.791
Can't you see that thing in front of her?

00:17:20.791 --> 00:17:23.710
I don't see anything.

00:17:32.928 --> 00:17:37.558
I've been looking for you, Michiko.
And now I've finally found you.

00:17:37.558 --> 00:17:39.685
That's your wife? You can't be serious.

00:17:39.685 --> 00:17:44.731
I'm positive. You think I wouldn't
recognize the love of my life?!

00:17:45.941 --> 00:17:50.320
I'm sorry it took so long. Now I'll be with you.

00:18:02.332 --> 00:18:04.084
Toriko!

00:18:06.461 --> 00:18:08.130
You're hurting me. Let go.

00:18:08.130 --> 00:18:08.964
No.

00:18:08.964 --> 00:18:12.050
I have to go... to Satsuki.

00:18:12.050 --> 00:18:13.594
Don't do this.

00:18:13.594 --> 00:18:17.890
Let me go to her. Satsuki's right there.

00:18:17.890 --> 00:18:20.350
No! Don't go, Toriko!

00:18:20.350 --> 00:18:23.937
Satsuki, Satsuki.

00:18:23.937 --> 00:18:28.108
Don't leave me here, you idiot!
Don't leave me all alone.

00:18:28.108 --> 00:18:29.610
I don't want you to go!

00:18:29.610 --> 00:18:32.237
No! Sorawo!

00:18:32.237 --> 00:18:33.697
What are you doing?

00:18:33.697 --> 00:18:36.617
I said, stay back! It's dangerous!
Can't you hear me?

00:18:36.617 --> 00:18:38.243
Huh?

00:18:44.958 --> 00:18:46.376
Get up, Sorawo.

00:18:46.376 --> 00:18:48.420
Wh-What just happened?

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:51.757
You were chasing Mr. Abarato, and then
you went straight toward that monster.

00:18:51.757 --> 00:18:54.301
You were mumbling weird things the whole time.

00:18:54.301 --> 00:18:57.179
I was the one it tricked? I don't get it.

00:18:57.179 --> 00:19:00.641
Just like Mr. Abarato was tricked
into thinking his wife was there,

00:19:00.641 --> 00:19:02.976
it was using my feelings against me.

00:19:02.976 --> 00:19:05.479
My feelings for whom?

00:19:05.479 --> 00:19:07.648
For Toriko?

00:19:07.648 --> 00:19:09.650
Aah! What the heck?

00:19:09.650 --> 00:19:10.692
Enough already!

00:19:10.692 --> 00:19:13.070
You kept saying, "Don't leave me all alone"
and "I don't want you to go."

00:19:13.070 --> 00:19:15.656
Sorawo, how do you think we can destroy her?

00:19:15.656 --> 00:19:18.450
H-How am I supposed to know?

00:19:22.913 --> 00:19:28.168
I can see. I recognize it for what it is. And...

00:19:31.713 --> 00:19:34.800
Toriko, aim for her head!

00:19:36.134 --> 00:19:39.513
So the bullets do hit home when I'm aware of it.

00:19:41.723 --> 00:19:43.433
I know! Take off that glove!

00:19:43.433 --> 00:19:45.060
Wh-What're you doing?

00:19:45.060 --> 00:19:47.104
Hey! Sorawo, what's going on?

00:19:47.104 --> 00:19:51.066
My right eye can see the true form
of monsters here on the Otherside.

00:19:51.066 --> 00:19:52.818
And your left hand...

00:19:52.818 --> 00:19:54.736
Sorry about this!

00:19:55.863 --> 00:19:56.738
Grab it!

00:19:56.738 --> 00:19:58.031
Grab what?

00:19:58.031 --> 00:20:01.994
Huh? I can't see it, but I feel
something. What am I grabbing?

00:20:01.994 --> 00:20:07.249
I knew it! Toriko, your left hand
can touch that creature!

00:20:35.319 --> 00:20:39.990
Birds are singing. I hear cicadas, too.

00:20:39.990 --> 00:20:45.412
Yeah, this isn't the Otherside.
We're back in our world.

00:20:45.412 --> 00:20:48.248
But where exactly?

00:20:51.251 --> 00:20:53.504
"Chichibu Shrine Bus Stop 30-Minute Walk"

00:20:53.712 --> 00:20:54.963
Oh, right.

00:20:54.963 --> 00:20:59.843
Mr. Abarato said he entered the
Otherside from the mountains of Chichibu.

00:21:00.928 --> 00:21:03.180
Let's head to the bus stop.

00:21:06.391 --> 00:21:12.022
Toriko, you didn't believe Satsuki was there?

00:21:12.022 --> 00:21:17.069
I did at first, but then
I realized what was happening.

00:21:17.069 --> 00:21:18.153
How?

00:21:18.153 --> 00:21:21.698
Good question. Maybe because you lost it first,

00:21:21.698 --> 00:21:23.367
and I couldn't bear to see you like that.

00:21:23.367 --> 00:21:27.663
Th-That was an illusion
that thing put in my head.

00:21:28.830 --> 00:21:31.083
Sorawo, you're such a handful.

00:21:31.083 --> 00:21:33.168
I better keep an eye on you
so you don't wander off.

00:21:33.168 --> 00:21:34.211
B-But...

00:21:34.211 --> 00:21:36.713
I could say the exact same thing about you!

00:21:36.713 --> 00:21:39.383
Hey, do you have your wallet?

00:21:39.383 --> 00:21:40.801
Huh?

00:21:48.141 --> 00:21:51.895
What? You don't have enough
for the bus ride home? Don't cry.

00:21:51.895 --> 00:21:54.439
What? Chichibu? Okay, listen up.

00:21:55.941 --> 00:21:57.401
"Surviving Lady Hasshaku"
You'll have to walk home.

00:21:57.401 --> 00:21:59.945
"Surviving Lady Hasshaku"
What?

00:21:59.945 --> 00:22:00.279
What?

00:23:32.246 --> 00:23:35.249
Ahhh! There's nothing better than
a cold beer after a 12-hour walk!

00:23:35.249 --> 00:23:35.374
"A celebration of survival"
Ahhh! There's nothing better than
a cold beer after a 12-hour walk!

00:23:35.374 --> 00:23:37.251
"A celebration of survival"
That took way too long.

00:23:37.251 --> 00:23:40.379
"A celebration of survival"
We ended up walking in circles
because I listened to you.

00:23:40.379 --> 00:23:41.713
"A celebration of survival"
I took a wrong turn.

00:23:41.713 --> 00:23:43.173
"A celebration of survival"
You need better planning skills.

00:23:43.173 --> 00:23:43.465
You need better planning skills.

00:23:43.465 --> 00:23:44.299
No thanks.

00:23:44.299 --> 00:23:47.072
This isn't really working.
